{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175081-question-initial-cover-and-angel-jacking","id":175081,"title":"[Question] Initial Cover and Angel-Jacking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-20T02:37:13-07:00","id":175081,"title":"[Question] Initial Cover and Angel-Jacking","content":"Hi! I'm a little late to the party, but I picked up DtD this week and have been enjoying it very much. A question about the usefulness of God-Machine fabricated Cover has been bugging me, so here is my dilemma. Initial Cover and Cover gained through Angel-Jacking are both produced by the God-Machine. Assuming this is true then what is the usefulness of said Cover? The God-Machine should be intimately familiar with the Cover of a demon in both cases, which doesn't seem like a good deal if you are looking to remain hidden. As soon as a suspicious report about an angel acting against its programming is made these Covers don't seem that useful. All the God-Machine needs to do is download information about a Cover it has created to a non-malfunctioning angel and said Cover should be blown. Or have I understood something wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T08:27:29-07:00","id":175258,"title":"","content":"One of the first things any demon that plans to <i>stay</i> a demon rather than recycled or dead does is &quot;jailbreak&quot; their Cover to prevent surveillance. Ostensibly this is related to the communications difficulties experienced by most exiles or the way demon-blooded backtracing works.<br /> <br /> It's possible to literally hack God's brain from the right terminals, it shouldn't be surprising that creatures with innate understandings of occult physics can manage something as simple as yanking out the wires they had in their pockets on their last job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-20-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T15:25:35-07:00","id":175581,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, the God-Machine doesn't pay complete attention to what all of their angels do - they're on far too small a scale to all be personally observed unless something's very wrong - and likewise other angels don't have access to all the information that the God-Machine has. Between these two facts there's a lot of stuff that just slips through the cracks.<br /> <br /> For angel-jacked characters, you're partially correct: angel-jacked covers start off with the Plugged-In Condition. A demon in one of these covers is under significant but not complete surveillance; while the God-Machine knows their physical location the entire time and the cover has a chance to be Blown, you're free to act inside the bounds of your cover without issue, and even if you do risk Compromise, you can let your cover Glitch out a little instead of blowing your cover. Once you've done the task the angel was created for, the Plugged-In Condition resolves because at that point your existence doesn't matter nearly as much anymore; the God-Machine disengages the tracking Infrastructure and assumes you'll come in (or be captured) for recycling. Once its scrutiny passes, it's easy to slip away and get gone in the masses.<br /> <br /> For initial covers, I like to think that Satchel has the right of it, and I go one step further and say that the metaphysical act of Falling twists and severs the Infrastructure that sustains and tracks the angelic Cover; it's impossible for the God-Machine to track that Cover because it's changed on a fundamental level, and it's possible that the God-Machine can't remember the old cover because of the trauma caused by it shearing away from the rest of Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T19:59:43-07:00","id":175700,"title":"","content":"Thank you both. I didn't think about the difficulty of making that initial report about an angel acting against its programming. So, unless a demon has the Plugged-In Condition, how would anyone know? I suppose a Command and Control or Defense Infrastructure connected to Intial Cover might raise a flag or two, but I don't see these going straight to the Blown Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T20:34:44-07:00","id":175744,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Like I said, I like to think that the Fall not only cuts the cover off from the God-Machine's support and tracking systems but also erases the information about it from its databases, metaphorically speaking. For every Demon that Falls in a hail of molten palladium and boneshards that alerts every loyalist within a ten mile radius there are probably three Demons that experience the Fall as an internal thing and just...walk away; if the forces of the God-Machine look into it, they're probably hours or days behind and they don't even know who they're looking for anymore, let alone where they are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T06:08:45-07:00","id":175959,"title":"","content":"One interesting thing to note about Cover is that they are a form of infrastructure of their own. In <i>Heirs to Hell </i>it off-hand mentions some details about an Unchained's cover. It says that a Cover masks a demon because it is a psychic veil that is cast over them that itself is created by the expectations of the humans around the demon. So long as the human believes that is &quot;Bob from Accounting&quot; reasonably, or &quot;that homeless guy in the park&quot; the Cover remains intact, expectations are met, and there are no unusual ripples in reality that alert the God-Machine to the oddity. This is why a demon, when living their Cover, doesn't actually have to 100% live their Cover's life (otherwise there'd be no time for Demon-y things!) but only has to create the <i>appearance to humans </i>that he is living his Cover's life.<br /> <br /> This is interesting because it suggests that Cover is the infrastructure that the God-Machine put it place to protect you as an angel, but you tore it away and <i>stole</i> it when you Fell. Like Satchel says, you jailbroke the Cover, and stole the work telephone-to-God to play video games at home. As a storyteller this has interesting implications and provides some interesting aspects of what a Fall might do to the God-Machine and why it is so &quot;noisy&quot;. If your Concealment Infrastructure was a park bench that had to be sat on every 3 hours to maintain the Occult Matrix that kept you hidden from human sight, then suddenly upon your fall, that bench is missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T07:56:20-07:00","id":176001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175081-question-initial-cover-and-angel-jacking?p=175959#post175959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One interesting thing to note about Cover is that they are a form of infrastructure of their own. In <i>Heirs to Hell </i>it off-hand mentions some details about an Unchained's cover. It says that a Cover masks a demon because it is a psychic veil that is cast over them that itself is created by the expectations of the humans around the demon. So long as the human believes that is &quot;Bob from Accounting&quot; reasonably, or &quot;that homeless guy in the park&quot; the Cover remains intact, expectations are met, and there are no unusual ripples in reality that alert the God-Machine to the oddity. This is why a demon, when living their Cover, doesn't actually have to 100% live their Cover's life (otherwise there'd be no time for Demon-y things!) but only has to create the <i>appearance to humans </i>that he is living his Cover's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>More to come on this topic in Flowers, which was written about a month before that paragraph in Heirs was, but you're on the right track. I'm pretty proud of the explanation of how Cover works in no small part because I really dig the &quot;conspicuously living a lie&quot; aspect of playing a demon (and the psychological horror it implies), and I think this reinforces that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}